Masume — attribution notice
===========================

This repository is public, which means the data in it is being distributed. The
obligations below follow from that, and they apply to the datasets rather than to
the application code.


Stroke order data — src/data/kvg-strokes.json
---------------------------------------------

Extracted from KanjiVG (https://kanjivg.tagaini.net/), by Ulrich Apel and
contributors, licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0.

Only the 150 characters this app draws were extracted, and only the stroke path
data; the paths themselves are unmodified.

KanjiVG was chosen over @k1low/hanzi-writer-data-jp because the latter derives from
Chinese font outlines and disagrees with Japanese handwriting convention on 21 of
those 150 characters. See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md.

The superseded licence texts for that package remain in
licenses/hanzi-writer-data-jp/ for reference; no data from it ships any more.


Kana dataset — src/data/kana.json
---------------------------------

Compiled for this project from the standard gojūon structure, and generated
deterministically by scripts/generate-kana.mjs. No third-party dataset was copied.


Vocabulary, kanji and grammar datasets — not yet in this repository
------------------------------------------------------------------

Planned for Phase 0 Sprint 2. When they land, they will derive from OpenJLPT, which
draws on:

  - JMdict / EDICT (Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group),
    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
  - KANJIDIC2 (EDRDG), Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
  - Jonathan Waller's JLPT level tables (tanos.co.uk),
    Creative Commons Attribution 3.0
  - Tatoeba example sentences, Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 France

Grammar points not present in OpenJLPT are written for this project and marked
"source": "compiled" in the data, as opposed to "source": "openjlpt". They are not
copied from Bunpro, JLPT Sensei, or any other commercial source.


